- op: discuss  # 7f0b
  at: '2026-04-02T14:27:52Z'  # 7f0b
  by: agent  # 7f0b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7f0b
  clock: 2  # 7f0b
  nonce: 7f0b  # 7f0b
  message: "Investigation: The pyffi linker only creates ffi_bridge edges against repo-local C symbols. When Python uses ffi.dlopen(None) to call C stdlib directly, there are no local C symbols to match — the linker needs to either (a) create unresolved edges similar to cgo pseudo-namespace pattern, or (b) the io_boundary tagger needs a Python-side catalog for ctypes/cffi stdlib calls. This is a design-level change, not a simple fix. Deprioritizing."  # 7f0b
- op: discuss  # 6dab
  at: '2026-04-02T14:43:06Z'  # 6dab
  by: human  # 6dab
  actor: jgstern  # 6dab
